                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "55457527",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561198062744185",
                            "num_reviews": 57,
                            "playtime_forever": 705,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 446,
                            "last_played": 1570346385
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "This game is really laggy during some battle scenes and it becomes unplayable and unpausable and must be closed. Walking during battles is frustrating sometimes because the characters choose to walk into other characters even when selecting what you think is the correct way around one. \n\nSo many random battles. Not enough random concepts, it seems theres just a handful of ideas of what your gonna get when you enter something. I did a few playthroughs and found I could remember almost every potential outcome because there was so few.\n\nMany loading screens and lag issues. Noticing many crashing errors now as well\n\nFun game, lots of potential but many issues make it frustrating",
                        "timestamp_created": 1570273835,
                        "timestamp_updated": 1570346666,
                        "voted_up": false,
                        "votes_up": 5,
                        "votes_funny": 0,
                        "weighted_vote_score": 0.5891830921173096,
                        "comment_count": 1,
                        "steam_purchase": true,
                        "received_for_free": false,
                        "written_during_early_access": false,
                        "developer_response": "Hi AirWit,\nThanks a lot for your comment. We are constantly trying to improve, and based on your feedback and others we've prepared a patch for tomorrow.\n\nAbout the characters colliding between them, it was a design decision. It was wrong, and with this patch heroes don't collide at all with other heroes. \nWe also have improved path finding against enemies. There is still collision with them, and we think is better that way, but now heroes are \"smarter\" finding the way without removing the challenge of positioning. In the end we want a challenge that is not frustrating.\n\nAbout load screens, we have reduced load time before combat. \n\nAbout performance in general, we tested it on low spec computers and performance was ok, but of course there are many different setups. Really sorry about that.\n\nWe also are preparing a DLC with more content, the possibility to start with thief and cleric and some other details.\n\nAnyway, I´m glad to hear that at least you had some fun and hope you give us other try at some point in time.",
                        "timestamp_dev_responded": 1570732158,
                        "primarily_steam_deck": false,
                        "refunded": false
                    }
                ],
